+## Self-check
+
+- **Regression FAILS reverted / PASSES fixed.** RED: build EXIT=2 (logs 02, 08, 18) and ctest EXIT=8 with
+  `Not Run` (09, 19); GREEN: build EXIT=0 and ctest EXIT=0, 1/1 (20/21, 23/25). The reverted compile under
+  Apple's predefines is EXIT=1 with the CI's `getpid`/`usleep` (22); with the fix EXIT=0 (24).
+- **Deterministic.** Compile-time contract only; no timing, sleep, thread or injected clock. The only
+  runtime assertion added by this branch is the pre-existing macro-value slot.
+- **At the cause, all siblings checked.** `include/RemotePluginBase.h` is the only in-tree definition site of
+  `SYNC_WITH_SHM_FIFO`; `rg "SYNC_WITH_SHM_FIFO"` shows consumers at `src/common/RemotePluginBase.cpp`,
+  `src/core/RemotePlugin.cpp` and the tests, all of which include the header rather than re-deriving the
+  includes. The socket branch's own `<unistd.h>` (`:82`) is unchanged, `<process.h>` for mingw is unchanged,
+  and the probe's crutch is gone so the header is exercised for real on every host. Every target that
+  includes the header was rebuilt (14): `zene`, the three RemotePlugin test targets, `FakeRemotePluginClient`,
+  `RemoteZynAddSubFx`, `NativeLinuxRemoteVstPlugin64`, plus `RemotePluginShmFifoCompileCheck`.
+- **No collateral damage.** The change adds one `#include <unistd.h>` under a config macro that POSIX hosts
+  already satisfied; no declaration, type, macro value, limit, serialized field, command, undo step or
+  audio-thread path changed. Windows keeps its branch (`LMMS_HAVE_UNISTD_H` is not defined there;
+  `DetectMachine.cmake:1-2` sets `LMMS_BUILD_WIN32`). Old projects cannot be affected: nothing touches
+  persistence.
+- **Realtime / undo / commands.** Header-only include; no new allocation, lock, wait, log or command. The
+  `usleep(5)` at `:459` is pre-existing and unchanged; no new call site was added.
+- **Gates.** 8/8 PASS, EXIT=0 (log 27, run with this report present): fork-sources, all-sources-reproduce,
+  no-upstream-regression, check-namespace, no-tautology, doc-figures, complexity, file-length.
+  `submit_check.py`'s own gates row is FAIL, and it is the lane's write policy, not a gate: that row runs the
+  unmodified `feature_check.py`, which dies before any gate on
+  `PermissionError: .../zene-qwen-ci-4e020460347493c3-feature-check` (log 30, EXIT=1) because it creates its
+  log directory next to the worktree. Run with only that directory redirected (log 27) the same script
+  exits 0 with the 8/8 table above; the gate scripts themselves are untouched.
+- **Sibling commands (submit_check ASK).** This fix touches no command file: the diff since the branch base
+  contains only `include/RemotePluginBase.h`, the probe source, the two registration files and this report.
+  The `app.*` / `arrangement.*` list submit_check prints comes from the train-wide `base..HEAD` diff (206
+  files) and not from this change; none of those commands, their handlers or `commands_snapshot.json` is
